---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/welcome-series';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/welcome-series');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/welcome-series');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Should every welcome contain a discount?",
    "answer": "Honor an advertised offer when eligible. Otherwise select content that meets the signup promise; a discount is optional."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can existing customers receive welcome?",
    "answer": "Yes. Welcome them as subscribers while avoiding ineligible first-order offers and inaccurate new-customer language."
  },
  {
    "question": "How long should the series run?",
    "answer": "Use only the messages needed for the signup promise and buying questions. Set spacing and an endpoint for the specific audience."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should happen after a purchase?",
    "answer": "Recheck queued acquisition messages and route appropriate product or subscriber education separately from authoritative order notifications."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24"><div class="container">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Welcome series</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify email tools for welcome series</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Welcome begins with the promise made at signup. Deliver the requested content or offer, explain what will arrive next, and route existing buyers differently from people considering a first purchase. An email address captured during checkout is not automatically a newsletter subscription.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary mt-9" href="/apps">Compare the tool catalog</a>
  </div></section>
  <article class="container pb-16 space-y-12">
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Carry the signup promise into the message</h2>
      <p>Store the form or source identifier, permission state, promised resource or incentive and any preference the customer explicitly supplied. Preserve the actual offer terms, including applicable items and expiry. A missing source needs a neutral fallback, not an invented discount promise.</p>
      <p>A proposed coffee-roaster welcome has separate entry routes for a brewing guide and a release newsletter. Guide subscribers receive the resource; release subscribers learn how announcements work. Neither route should claim a reserved bag or a position in a queue unless another system actually provides it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Separate first purchase from subscriber welcome</h2>
      <p>A returning buyer can still deserve a welcome after subscribing. Acknowledge their relationship without an ineligible first-order offer. Check order history and identity matching, including guest orders and an address change, before assuming someone has never bought.</p>
      <p>Klaviyo documents a welcome-series conditional split based on whether an order was placed since starting the flow. That can route later content after a purchase; it does not replace checking earlier order history when deciding first-order eligibility. Keep those two questions separate in the flow design.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Sequence by the unresolved question</h2>
      <p>After delivering the promise, choose content that answers the next obstacle: shipping policy, compatibility, product selection or how the subscription works. Set spacing from the buying decision and observed feedback rather than a universal number of messages. Remove a message when it adds no new information.</p>
      <p>For a keyboard parts store, explain layout and switch compatibility using maintained product references before offering a bundle. For a content newsletter, show a representative issue and frequency. Do not label someone as discount-sensitive because they have not opened a message; opens are an uncertain proxy for intent.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Protect the offer across simultaneous flows</h2>
      <p>A new subscriber may purchase immediately or start a cart while welcome is queued. Recheck offer eligibility and suppress a redundant acquisition pitch after purchase. Choose how welcome education and cart assistance coexist; a relevant guide need not disappear simply because an offer message is paused.</p>
      <p>Record which workflow owns any code and how the checkout validates it. Prevent duplicate incentives with shared eligibility rules, not copy claiming codes cannot stack. Confirmation, shipping and access instructions remain in their authoritative order systems rather than depending on completion of marketing welcome.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Evaluate source changes and re-entry</h2>
      <p>Compare capture and sending tools separately. In a demonstration of Privy, Klaviyo, Omnisend, Drip or Sequenzy, trace your actual source field, permission update, offer and order event. A template preview does not establish that the capture integration preserves those fields.</p>
      <p>Proposed exercises include a renamed form, missing source, repeat submission, existing buyer and purchase during a delay. Confirm the promised resource arrives once and later offers match eligibility. Compare first-order conversion and contribution by signup source, with a declared observation window; do not credit all subsequent purchases to welcome.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card"><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Reference and related workflows</h2>
      <p>Product reference: <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002775172">Klaviyo welcome series setup</a>. Workflow recommendations and proposed exercises above are editorial guidance.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/use-cases/segmentation">segmentation</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">post purchase</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Welcome series FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
